@startuml Tseten Deployment Architecture
!define RECTANGLE_WIDTH 280
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam wrapWidth 250
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

title Tseten - Deployment Architecture

skinparam node {
    BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
    BorderColor #1976D2
}

skinparam component {
    BackgroundColor #BBDEFB
    BorderColor #1565C0
}

skinparam database {
    BackgroundColor #C8E6C9
    BorderColor #388E3C
}

skinparam cloud {
    BackgroundColor #FFF9C4
    BorderColor #F57F17
}

actor "End User" as user

cloud "Web Browser" {
    component "Angular 19 SPA" as spa {
        **Tseten.App**
        ====
        - TypeScript 5.6
        - Angular Material UI
        - Standalone components
        - Served as static files
        ----
        Build: ng build --configuration production
        Output: dist/ folder
    }
}

node "Application Server" {
    component "ASP.NET Core 8.0" as api {
        **Tseten.Api**
        ====
        - .NET 8.0 Runtime
        - Kestrel web server
        - HTTPS (port 7157)
        - HTTP (port 5000)
        ----
        Run: dotnet run
        Deploy: dotnet publish -c Release
    }
    
    component "Tseten.Core" as core {
        **Domain Library**
        ====
        - Business logic
        - Domain models
        - Validators
    }
    
    component "Tseten.Infrastructure" as infra {
        **Infrastructure Library**
        ====
        - Data access
        - External services
        - Authentication
    }
}

node "Data Server" {
    database "Couchbase Lite" as couchbase {
        **Embedded Database**
        ====
        - NoSQL document store
        - File-based: *.cblite2
        - Located in app directory
        ----
        Collections:
        - software-requirements
        - tags
        - users
        - profiles
    }
    
    database "SQL Server / SQL Express" as sqlserver {
        **Relational Database**
        ====
        - Vector embeddings storage
        - TsetenVectorDb database
        ----
        Connection String:
        Server=.\\SQLEXPRESS;
        Database=TsetenVectorDb;
        Trusted_Connection=true;
        ----
        Tables:
        - Embeddings (384-dim vectors)
    }
}

' User interactions
user --> spa : HTTPS\nhttps://localhost:4200

' API communication
spa --> api : REST API\nJSON over HTTPS\nhttps://localhost:7157/api

' Internal dependencies
api --> core : uses
api --> infra : uses
infra --> core : uses

' Data access
infra --> couchbase : Couchbase.Lite.dll\nEmbedded access
infra --> sqlserver : EF Core\nTCP/IP connection

note right of spa
**Static Hosting Options**
- Development: ng serve
- Production: nginx, IIS, Azure Static Web Apps
- Build artifacts in dist/ folder
- Environment-specific configs

**CORS Configuration**
Backend must allow frontend origin:
WithOrigins("http://localhost:4200")
end note

note bottom of api
**Hosting Options**
- Development: dotnet run
- Windows: IIS with ASP.NET Core Module
- Linux: Kestrel with reverse proxy (nginx)
- Docker: Container deployment
- Azure: App Service, Container Apps

**Configuration**
- appsettings.json (base)
- appsettings.Development.json
- appsettings.Production.json
- Environment variables
end note

note right of couchbase
**Embedded Database**
No separate server process needed.
Database files stored locally with app.
Perfect for single-machine deployment.

**Backup**
Backup *.cblite2 directory periodically.
end note

note right of sqlserver
**Vector Database**
Requires SQL Server or SQL Express.
Can be on same or different machine.

**Setup**
1. Create database: TsetenVectorDb
2. EF Core migrations apply schema
3. Configure connection string

**Alternatives**
- Azure SQL Database (cloud)
- PostgreSQL with pgvector
- Separate vector DB (Pinecone, Weaviate)
end note

== Development Environment ==

package "Developer Machine" {
    node "Dev Setup" {
        [Visual Studio / VS Code]
        [.NET 8 SDK]
        [Node.js 18+ / npm]
        [SQL Server Express]
    }
}

note bottom of "Dev Setup"
**Development Setup Steps**
1. Install .NET 8 SDK
2. Install Node.js 18+
3. Install SQL Server Express
4. Clone repository
5. Backend: dotnet restore, dotnet run
6. Frontend: npm install, ng serve
7. Run migrations for SQL Server
8. Seed database with sample data
end note

@enduml
